e the same emotional dramatic  or comedic power as the best of Pixar  it's a minor entry in the Pixar Canon a  perfectly pleasant way to pass the time  however although onward received kudos  for the performances of Holland Pratt  and Spencer in particular and for  hitting those familiar emotional notes  we crave from Pixar den of geeks David  crow remarks whatever its shortcomings  onward is still an amusing Lee clever  piece of family entertainment with a  tangible hearth of the center of his  book of spouse this might be Pixar on an  off day  but even that it feels like spending  quality time with a dear loved one a  fairly strong contingent of  viewers for quite a bit less forgiving I  see you've brought sustenance for our  adventure no it's garbage for the trash  can  they tend it to peg on word is  half-baked too long and well extremely  weird in an off-putting way Mick LaSalle  of the San Francisco Chronicle wrote on  what looks great and as a couple of  strong scenes on the Crippin and even  ingenious births as a whole the movie is  misbegotten over long and all together  and convincing as a story of familial  love long before it's 114 minute running  time has elapsed in his over status  welcome Mike Ryan of aprox was even less  kind this is a movie about two kids  resurrecting their dead dad's crotch and  it's just the weirdest thing at one  point in this movie I literally tried to  get emotional if I'm watching nothing I  can make myself get there watching  onwards I couldn't do it every time I  felt even a hint of emotion here comes a  walking crotch other reviewers slapped  on word with labels such as undercooked  flattened and diluted and  disappointingly pedestrian the consensus  of on words negative notices was summed  up nicely by Josh Spiegel of / film  onward is OK  the problem with onward is that Pixar's  original films are incredible okay it's  simply just not good enough  the majority of critics though found  onward to be a satisfactory if  unsp